DECISION: phase_e2_normalization_pairing_ablation_complete
VALUE:     Ground-truth LyASC+LN baseline confirmed as Phase D closed-out result: 7.17% ± 0.21% (seeds 7.33%, 7.25%, 6.93%). Reused without retraining. LyASC_noG (G=Identity) test error = 9.52% ± 0.98% (+2.35pp penalty vs LyASC+LN 7.17%); LyASC+BN (G=BatchNorm2d) test error = 6.34% ± 0.01% (observed difference of -0.83pp vs LyASC+LN 7.17%).
RATIONALE: Baseline Audit & Phase E2 normalization pairing ablations completed (depth 110, 64k iters, 2 seeds each):
1. Baseline Audit & Provenance Verification: Reused pre-registered Phase D cold-start 'none' baseline for LyASC+LN (3-seed mean: 7.17% ± 0.21%, seeds 0-2: 7.33%, 7.25%, 6.93%). No retraining performed. Provenance check confirmed draft table figures (6.31%, 6.32%, 6.39%) were pulled from base paper reference values; ground-truth 7.17% baseline restored.
2. LyASC_noG (G=Identity, no post-gate norm): Seed 0 = 10.21%, Seed 1 = 8.82% (2-seed mean: 9.52% ± 0.98%, alpha_mean = 0.6580). Omitting post-gate normalization incurs a +2.35pp penalty vs LyASC+LN (7.17%), confirming post-gate normalization is necessary.
3. LyASC+BN (G=BatchNorm2d): Seed 0 = 6.35%, Seed 1 = 6.33% (2-seed mean: 6.34% ± 0.01%, alpha_mean = 0.5621). In unstressed training, this represents an observed difference of -0.83pp vs LyASC+LN (7.17%, n=3). This result is statistically indistinguishable from plain 1xSkip (6.27%-6.36%) and remains above 2rSkip+LN (6.15%). The behavior of LyASC+BN under stress conditions remains untested.
------------------------------------------------------------------------
